{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 15, :comments ["<b>Behold, he travails</b> — like \"your mother travailed with you\" (Hosea 13:13), before travail comes." "<b>And is pregnant with trouble</b> — the meaning is that its beginning is vanity and its end is breath, for all his plots will come to nothing and will not be."], :book :psalms, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 7, :notes {0 "The comparison is to the root ח-ב-ל in the sense of labor/birthing."}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Psalms -- Daat" "http://www.daat.ac.il/he-il/tanach/parshanut_hamikra/full-text/eben-ezra/tehilim"] ["Wikisource Mikraot Gedolot" "http://en.wikisource.org/wiki/Mikraot_Gedolot/"] ["Tanakh, Venice, 1617-1619" "https://dlib.rsl.ru/viewer/01007514045#?page=4"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T19:26:33.929296946Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}